. * ================================================================
. * H4 Analysis: Final Single-Test Version (Based on Revised PAP)
. * ================================================================
. * NOTE: Per project requirements, the analysis was restricted to a single
. * regression-based test. We selected 'plh0395i05' as the primary dependent
. * variable and the 'same-gender children only' specification with an
. * interaction term as the primary model, as outlined in our revised PAP.
. * ================================================================
. 
. use "$DATA/h4_data_final.dta", clear
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
. * --- Step 1: Create the sample and variables for the chosen test ---
. * Restrict sample to parents with only same-gender children
. keep if share_daughters == 0 | share_daughters == 1
(742 observations deleted)

. * Create the primary independent variable and the moderator
. gen has_only_daughters = (share_daughters == 1)

. gen male = (sex == 1)

. 
. * --- Step 2: Define variables for the single chosen test ---
. local dv "plh0395i05" // The single DV selected in the revised PAP

. local ind_vars "i.has_only_daughters##i.male age age_sq sampreg is_german pgb
> ilzeit"

. 
. * --- Step 3: Prepare the single CSV file ---
. file open myfile using "$OUT/h4_results.csv", write replace
(file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived/5_res
    > ults/h4_results.csv not found)

. //file write myfile "dependent_var,coef,se,family,residual_df,p_value,num_obs
> ,num_participants,interpretation" _n
. file write myfile "coefficient,se,family,residual_df,model_df,p_value,num_obs
> ,num_participants,interpretation" _n //Adapted by DA to ensure consistent exp
> ort of results.

. 
. * --- Step 4: Run the single, chosen model ---
. di ""


. di "*************************************************************************
> *******"
*******************************************************************************
> *

. di "Processing Final H4 Model for: `dv' (Same-Gender Interaction)"
Processing Final H4 Model for: plh0395i05 (Same-Gender Interaction)

. di "*************************************************************************
> *******"
*******************************************************************************
> *

. 
. * We use OLS with robust SE to test the interaction term
. reg `dv' `ind_vars', vce(robust)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        503
                                                F(8, 494)         =       3.39
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0009
                                                R-squared         =     0.0480
                                                Root MSE          =     1.9358

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
  plh0395i05 | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
1.has_only~s |   .4615427   .2245145     2.06   0.040     .0204216    .9026637
      1.male |   -.559383   .2611354    -2.14   0.033    -1.072456   -.0463098
             |
has_only_d~s#|
        male |
        1 1  |  -.0382178   .3484881    -0.11   0.913    -.7229194    .6464839
             |
         age |   .0455158   .0411833     1.11   0.270    -.0354002    .1264318
      age_sq |  -.0003327   .0003534    -0.94   0.347    -.0010271    .0003616
     sampreg |  -.1545497    .212199    -0.73   0.467    -.5714735    .2623741
   is_german |   .1225045   .3012909     0.41   0.684    -.4694651    .7144741
   pgbilzeit |   .0688703   .0325527     2.12   0.035     .0049114    .1328292
       _cons |   2.940267   1.192335     2.47   0.014      .597593     5.28294
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. * --- Step 5: Extract and export results for the INTERACTION TERM ---
. if _rc == 0 {
.     capture {
.     if _rc == 0 {
.         local test_stat_family "t"
.         local df_residual = e(df_r)
.         local t_stat = `coefficient' / `se'
.         local p_value = 2 * ttail(`df_residual', abs(`t_stat'))
.         local num_obs = e(N)
.         quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)
.         local num_participants : word count `participants'
.         
.         * For H4, a POSITIVE interaction coefficient is in line with the hypo
> thesis
.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"
. 
.         file write myfile "`coefficient',`se',`test_stat_family',`df_residual
> ',,`p_value',`num_obs',`num_participants',`interpretation'" _n
.     }
.     else {
.         di "Model for `dv' ran, but interaction term was dropped. Result not 
> saved."
.     }
. }

. else {
.     di "Model for `dv' failed to run (e.g. no observations). Result not saved
> ."
. }

. 
. * --- Step 6: Close the file ---
. file close myfile

. 
. di ""


. di "Final analysis for H4 complete. Results saved in 'h4_final_results.csv'."
Final analysis for H4 complete. Results saved in 'h4_final_results.csv'.

